kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[2]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,tui65,"thinking-text-via-markdown","The TUI MUST render finalized ThinkingText through the shared MarkdownRenderer (same as UserInput/AssistantText since c355), via a dedicated MarkdownStyle (for_thinking) that preserves the dim/italic visual hierarchy of reasoning content while still parsing code blocks, lists, and inline formatting. The streaming mutable thinking line stays plain text (spec tui61 streaming-stays-plain still holds); markdown rendering applies only after a thinking line is finalized and committed to scrollback. Evidence: codex AgentMarkdownCell does not distinguish thinking vs text in markdown parsing (only styling); pi shares one Markdown class across thinking/assistant with style parameters; current render.rs:81 ThinkingText branch bypasses render_markdown entirely.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui66,"blockquote-visual-prefix","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render blockquote lines with a visible leading prefix glyph (e.g. a left-bar like ▎) colored with the quote style, so blockquotes are distinguishable from plain paragraph text on terminals where the dim color difference is hard to perceive. The prefix MUST appear on every physical row of the blockquote (including wrapped continuation rows), and MUST indent for nested blockquotes (each nesting level adds another prefix). Evidence: codex uses a │ left bar for blockquotes; pi keeps the > prefix; kimi-code uses ▏ dim prefix; the c355 blockquote renderer applies only dim style with no glyph, which TestBackend visualization confirmed is visually indistinguishable from normal text.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[4]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui65,"thinking-renders-markdown",a finalized ThinkingText line containing a fenced code block is committed to scrollback,the line is rendered,"the code block renders with language label and structure (markdown parsed), styled dim/italic to distinguish from the main reply, verified via TestBackend"
  tui65,"thinking-source-shares-renderer",the RenderedLine source is inspected,the ThinkingText rendering path is read,"it calls MarkdownRenderer via to_lines (not to_line plain), differing from AssistantText only in the injected MarkdownStyle"
  tui66,"blockquote-has-prefix",an assistant reply containing a blockquote is finalized and rendered via TestBackend,"the buffer is inspected","each row of the blockquote carries a leading prefix glyph (▎) colored with the quote style, present on wrapped continuation rows too"
  tui66,"nested-blockquote-indents",a nested blockquote (>> ) is rendered via TestBackend,"the buffer is inspected","the inner blockquote rows carry an additional prefix glyph so nesting is visually expressed"
